  "result": "Perfect! All **356 tests pass** (10 new mergeCustomers tests added).\n\n**New Function: `mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)`**\n\nThe function removes a duplicate customer and reassigns all its invoices to another customer:\n- Returns `ok({ customers, invoices })` on success\n- Normalizes customer IDs (case-insensitive, trimmed)\n- Errors:\n  - `SAME_CUSTOMER` if both IDs refer to the same customer\n  - `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` if either ID doesn't exist\n- Filters out the `fromId` customer\n- Updates all invoices with `fromId` to point to `intoId`\n- Does not mutate input arrays\n\n**Updated: `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `SAME_CUSTOMER: 'Cannot merge a customer with itself.'`\n\n**New Tests: `test/customers.test.js`** (11 test cases)\n- Basic merge removes customer and migrates invoices\n- Input array immutability\n- Rejection of same customer (with case-insensitive handling)\n- Rejection of missing customer (fromId or intoId)\n- Preservation of customer order\n- Edge cases: no invoices to merge, many invoices to merge\n- Case-insensitive customer ID handling",
